{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following PyPy 3 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original PyPy 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nfrom itertools import product\n\nprimes = []\nfor p in range(2, 6000):\n    is_prime = True\n    for q in primes:\n        if q * q > p:\n            break\n        if p % q == 0:\n            is_prime = False\n            break\n    if is_prime:\n        primes.append(p)\n\ndef factor(n):\n    d = {}\n    for p in primes:\n        if p * p > n:\n            break\n        if n % p == 0:\n            c = 0\n            while n % p == 0:\n                n //= p\n                c += 1\n            d[p] = c\n    if n > 1:\n        d[n] = 1\n    return d\n\ndef divisors(n):\n    factor_dict = factor(n)\n    power_lists = []\n    for p, e in factor_dict.items():\n        power_lists.append([p ** k for k in range(e + 1)])\n    divs = []\n    for combo in product(*power_lists):\n        value = 1\n        for pw in combo:\n            value *= pw\n        divs.append(value)\n    return divs\n\ndef process(n, m):\n    f = {0: 0, 1: 1, 2: 2}\n    for i in range(3, n + 1):\n        f[i] = 2 * f[i - 1]\n        for x in divisors(i):\n            if 2 <= x <= i:\n                f[i] = (f[i] + f[i // x] - f[(i - 1) // x]) % m\n        f[i] %= m\n    return f[n]\n\nn, m = [int(x) for x in input().split()]\nprint(process(n, m))\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <map>\n#include <cmath>\n#include <algorithm>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nvector<int> primes;\n\nvoid precompute_primes() {\n    for (int p = 2; p < 6000; ++p) {\n        bool is_prime = true;\n        for (int q : primes) {\n            if (q * q > p) break;\n            if (p % q == 0) {\n                is_prime = false;\n                break;\n            }\n        }\n        if (is_prime) primes.push_back(p);\n    }\n}\n\nmap<int,int> factor(int n) {\n    map<int,int> d;\n    for (int p : primes) {\n        if (p * p > n) break;\n        if (n % p == 0) {\n            int c = 0;\n            while (n % p == 0) {\n                n /= p;\n                ++c;\n            }\n            d[p] = c;\n        }\n    }\n    if (n > 1) d[n] = 1;\n    return d;\n}\n\nvoid generate_divisors(const map<int,int>& factors, vector<long long>& divs) {\n    divs.clear();\n    divs.push_back(1);\n    for (auto& entry : factors) {\n        int p = entry.first;\n        int e = entry.second;\n        long long pow_p = 1;\n        vector<long long> new_divs;\n        for (int k = 0; k <= e; ++k) {\n            for (long long d : divs) {\n                new_divs.push_back(d * pow_p);\n            }\n            pow_p *= p;\n        }\n        divs.swap(new_divs);\n    }\n}\n\nvector<long long> divisors(int n) {\n    map<int,int> fac = factor(n);\n    vector<long long> divs;\n    generate_divisors(fac, divs);\n    return divs;\n}\n\nlong long process(int n, long long m) {\n    vector<long long> f(n+1);\n    f[0] = 0;\n    if (n >= 1) f[1] = 1;\n    if (n >= 2) f[2] = 2;\n    for (int i = 3; i <= n; ++i) {\n        f[i] = (2 * f[i-1]) % m;\n        vector<long long> divs = divisors(i);\n        for (long long x : divs) {\n            if (x >= 2 && x <= i) {\n                long long term = (f[i / x] - f[(i - 1) / x] + m) % m;\n                f[i] = (f[i] + term) % m;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    return f[n] % m;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    precompute_primes();\n    int n;\n    long long m;\n    cin >> n >> m;\n    cout << process(n, m) << endl;\n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-3.58813522325363e-05, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.00038246947224251926, -0.0003672163875307888, -2.264974000354414e-06, -0.0015047191409394145, -1.1444026313256472e-05, 0.0, 0.0, -4.768370445162873e-07, -9.536738616588991e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -0.3871750831604004, -6.318072337307967e-06, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.04860879108309746, -0.10023494809865952, -0.014163684099912643, 0.0, -0.0005544078885577619, -0.06198554113507271, -0.024693869054317474, -2.9802276912960224e-06, 0.0, -4.684815212385729e-05, -0.22092780470848083, -0.006715348921716213, 0.0, -0.0002256377338198945, -0.008640403859317303, -0.04859800264239311, -0.9722676873207092, -1.645074735279195e-05, -0.008625631220638752, 0.0, -0.04859277978539467, -3.576278118089249e-07, -1.311301275563892e-06, -0.33897724747657776, -2.1457441107486375e-05, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -4.0531076592742465e-06, -1.6689160474925302e-05, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -0.004218014422804117, 0.0, -7.152555099310121e-07, -1.0728830375228426e-06, 0.0, -0.004079116974025965, -3.576278118089249e-07, 0.0, -4.768370445162873e-07, 0.0, -8.344646857949556e-07, -0.00022539935889653862, -0.00027450130437500775, 0.0, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -5.006777428206988e-06, 0.0, -0.0009274948388338089, -1.9073468138230965e-06, -1.6689286894688848e-06, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -3.576278118089249e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-0